# Pawnstar opening set, for self-play data generation (tools/gen_data.cpp --openings).
#
# Generated by tools/gen_openings.cpp (Pawnstar 1.2.8) from THIS ENGINE'S OWN PLAY: no
# book, no third party's data. 114419 lines of uniformly random legal moves were played
# from the start position, each to a ply drawn uniformly from [8, 12], and the position
# the line ended at was kept when it was not in check and the static NNUE evaluation of it was
# within 125 centipawns of the net's evaluation of the start position (158 cp,
# White's perspective; net nnue/pawnstar-v12.bin). Duplicates were dropped on the Zobrist key. One
# position per line played, so no two openings here share a line - and the count is a parameter,
# not a ceiling of the source.
#
# seed 1; kept 30000 of 114419 lines (51 died, 1392 in check or terminal, 82976
# unbalanced, 0 duplicate). The generator is deterministic: the same seed,
# options and net reproduce this file exactly, which is the audit trail for a set with no
# external source.
#
# A CAMPAIGN WANTS A BIGGER POOL THAN THIS. Generate one to a path of its own rather than
# committing it, and point gen_data at it:
#     build/gen_openings ~/pawnstar_nnue/openings-1m.epd 1000000 1
#
# One position per line, as the first four FEN fields. Lines beginning with '#' are comments:
# tools/gen_data.cpp skips them, and tools/run_sprt.sh strips them before handing the file to
# fastchess, whose EPD reader does not.
